((markdown:paragraph ((key . 0)) "First.\n") #(markdown:rule ((key . 1))) (markdown:paragraph ((key . 2)) "Second " (markdown:strong () "b") "\n"))
; In a buffer, a block that grows at its end grows by an insertion: a
; cursor and an anchor in a code block streaming line by line stay
; where they were.
> (import (chat))
> (show! chat:chat)
> (chat:receive! "Code:\n\n```scheme\n(define (f x)\n")
> (datums chat:chat)
((chat:reply () (markdown:paragraph ((key . 0)) "Code:\n") (markdown:code-block ((key . 1) (language . "scheme")) "(define (f x)\n")))
